# ssh-cert-api is a position-independent EXECUTABLE (built with -buildmode=pie),
# so it is ET_DYN and lintian misclassifies it as a shared library. It is a
# program, not a library: it has no SONAME and no library prerequisites.
cerberus-api: shared-library-lacks-prerequisites [usr/bin/ssh-cert-api]

# The service env file is shipped 0640 (not world-readable) on purpose, matching
# the RPM/Arch packaging. systemd reads the EnvironmentFile as root, so the
# restricted mode is defense-in-depth.
#
# The config template is deliberately NOT listed here: it now ships 0644 under
# /usr/share, where a restricted mode would be anomalous and buys nothing -- it
# carries no secrets and is public in the source repository.
cerberus-api: non-standard-file-perm 0640 != 0644 [etc/default/cerberus-api]
